  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/tree/master/src/Abblix.SharedSignals.Redis",
  "published": "2026-11-27T06:45:54.71Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A transmitter that runs as more than one replica needs a queue that every replica sees the same way. This outbox keeps each stream's pending events in Redis list and hash structures and performs enqueue, claim and acknowledge as atomic server-side operations, so two replicas cannot deliver the same event twice or lose one between them - which a queue over a plain distributed cache cannot promise. Drop-in for the default in-process outbox. Nothing in this package changes in 3.1; it ships with the 3.1 line. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v3.1",
